BUG: the weekYear plugin ignores the case where the week of a January date belongs to the previous week-year. For the en-gb locale (yearStart: 4, weekStart: 1), 2021-01-01/02/03 are in week 53 of week-year 2020, but `weekYear()` returns 2021. Expected 2020.

EXACT FIX: replace the whole file /dayjs/src/plugin/weekYear/index.js with exactly:

export default (o, c) => {
  const proto = c.prototype
  proto.weekYear = function () {
    const month = this.month()
    const weekOfYear = this.week()
    const year = this.year()
    if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
      return year + 1
    }
    if (month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52) {
      return year - 1
    }
    return year
  }
}

(2-space indent, no semicolons. The only change is the new `if (month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52) { return year - 1 }` block.)

